@startuml
title APT-SD-D05 Normal Cashier-Assisted Payment Sequence
skinparam shadowing false

actor Cashier
participant "Assisted Payment Terminal" as APT
participant "Central PMS" as Central
participant "Vendor PMS Connector" as Connector
participant "Vendor PMS / HCP" as Vendor
participant "Payment Orchestrator" as Pay
participant "Payment Provider" as Provider
participant "Site POS Server" as POS

Cashier -> APT : scan / enter ticket or card reference
APT -> Central : lookup request with device/cashier/shift/scope
Central -> Connector : live session / fee resolve
Connector -> Vendor : vendor lookup + fee calculation
Vendor --> Connector : session + fee facts
Connector --> Central : normalized result
Central -> Central : record payable basis
Central --> APT : display payable basis
Cashier -> APT : initiate payment
APT -> Central : payment initiation request
Central -> Pay : start provider workflow
Pay -> Provider : provider interaction
Provider --> Pay : provider outcome evidence
Pay --> Central : verified provider outcome
Central -> Central : record payment finality
Central -> POS : request Sales Invoice issuance
POS --> Central : fiscal identity/status
Central -> Central : record fiscal reference
Central -> Central : issue ExitAuthorization if eligible
Central --> APT : display payment/fiscal/exit status

note bottom
APT initiates and displays.
Central PMS owns finality and ExitAuthorization.
POS Server owns Sales Invoice issuance.
end note
@enduml
